<title>UK: UK Nov net consumer credit up s/a 1.105 bln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Nov net consumer credit up s/a 1.105 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally-adjusted consumer credit data.</p>
<p>-NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN stg)</p>
<p>					    Nov	 Oct	     Nov 95</p>
<p> Total net lending		    2,825     2,721 (2,631)  1,887</p>
<p> -- Consumer credit		   1,105	 875 (856)	600</p>
<p> -- On dwellings			1,720     1,846 (1,775)  1,286</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF NET CONSUMER LENDING BY SOURCE</p>
<p> -- Banks				 868	 634  (622)	 472</p>
<p> -- Building Soc			 23	  34  (35)	   33</p>
<p> -- Other specialist lenders	213	 207  (199)	 129</p>
<p> -- Retailers			     2	   3  (2)	   -30</p>
<p> -- Insurance co			 -1	  -3  (-2)	   -4</p>
<p> -- Credit card			 339	 281  (257)	 138</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted in pct)</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	    1.5	 1.2  (1.2)	 0.9</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  18.4	18.2 (18.0)     14.2</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  18.0	16.9 (16.8)     13.7</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     16.6	16.0 (16.0)     13.4</p>
<p> Total Personal borrowing mth/mth 0.6	 0.6  (0.6)	 0.4</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  7.1	 7.0  (6.7)	 5.2</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  6.8	 6.7  (6.5)	 5.1</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     6.3	 6.1  (6.1)	 5.4</p>
<p> Secured on Dwellings mth/mth     0.4	 0.5  (0.4)	 0.3</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  5.2	 5.2  (4.9)	 3.8</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  5.0	 5.0  (4.8)	 3.8</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     4.7	 4.6  (4.5)	 4.2</p>
<p>Note - Consensus forecast was for a 945 million stg rise in net credit.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
